Subject: PumpEffect: do not crash when a "your choice of keyword" pump has lost its target
Why: With 0004 the AI casts Practiced Offense, and 5 of the 1,000 patched Azorius Momo gauntlet
  games ended in an engine error: when the creature target is removed in response, the spell
  still resolves (its player target is legal), and PumpEffect.resolve asks for the keyword
  choice with tgtCards.get(0) on an empty list (IndexOutOfBoundsException). Any KWChoice pump
  whose target is gone hits it; it only showed up now because the AI never cast the card
  before. The guard matches the `!tgtCards.isEmpty()` check a few lines further down: with no
  target left, nothing is pumped, as the rules say. Java code: needs a Maven rebuild.
Measured: the 5 Azorius Momo gauntlet games that crashed with 0003-0007 (same command as in
  0003, seed 1; two against Azorius Control, three against Izzet Spellementals) were replayed
  with 0008 added by resuming a copy of that run: all 5 now finish (2 won, 3 lost), and the arm
  comes to 542-458 over all 1,000 games, 54.2% (95% CI 51-57%), with no engine errors. The other
  995 games cannot be affected: the changed branch always crashed before. Built with Maven in 49 s.

diff --git a/forge-game/src/main/java/forge/game/ability/effects/PumpEffect.java b/forge-game/src/main/java/forge/game/ability/effects/PumpEffect.java
index e20d73b..f259ad8 100644
--- a/forge-game/src/main/java/forge/game/ability/effects/PumpEffect.java
+++ b/forge-game/src/main/java/forge/game/ability/effects/PumpEffect.java
@@ -294,7 +294,7 @@ public class PumpEffect extends SpellAbilityEffect {
         List<String> keywords = Lists.newArrayList();
         if (sa.hasParam("KW")) {
             keywords.addAll(Arrays.asList(sa.getParam("KW").split(" & ")));
-        } else if (sa.hasParam("KWChoice")) {
+        } else if (sa.hasParam("KWChoice") && !tgtCards.isEmpty()) {
             List<String> options = Arrays.asList(sa.getParam("KWChoice").split(","));
             String chosen = activator.getController().chooseKeywordForPump(options, sa,
                     Localizer.getInstance().getMessage("lblChooseKeyword"), tgtCards.get(0));
